{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/415916-irem-and-distant-trade","id":415916,"title":"Irem and Distant Trade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-22T17:43:19-08:00","id":415916,"title":"Irem and Distant Trade","content":"Some pseudoarcheologists suggest that Egypt may have had trans-atlantic trade during the ancient past. Did Irem engage in any sort of ancient trade network? The passages in the dark era preview imply that the Ubar conflict was a world war sort of thing, so I'm trying to imagine other national entities that may have been aware of or involved in the dispute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:48:51-08:00","id":415999,"title":"","content":"Irem clearly got well into Mesopotamia; beyond that, it's up to individual Storytellers. Personally, the furthest I have Irem going is into Iran to conquer some proto-Scythians. The Transatlantic exploration would definitely be in theme, and I'd love to have trade with some Naga in India and the semi-mythical Xia Dynasty of China.<br /> <br /> The rest of the world deserves to be just as crazy-weird as Irem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T06:13:12-08:00","id":416437,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the idea of Irem as the proto-empire standing alone. Having other similiar entities undermines the radical shift they represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T17:04:02-08:00","id":416981,"title":"","content":"I've been treating Irem has having exploratory outposts scattered all over the planet, at least one per continent with Europe, Africa, and South Western Asia having more.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about the Naga, or Xia Dynasty to use them accurately. But they are now on my reading list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T17:09:32-08:00","id":416985,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm starting to picture a very colonial setup. I like to imagine Irem as sort of an 'English Empire', with a small geographical footprint but immense extended influence over trade and commerce leveraged via superior technology. It would be neat if they traded with the Norte Chico and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T17:39:53-08:00","id":417003,"title":"","content":"My depictions of Irem almost invariably look at it through the eyes of the player characters, so I haven't really bothered to think about it outside of that context. The City of Pillars itself, and their lives within it, are really the only elements I have mapped out. As a consequence, my own version of Irem is remarkably self-absorbed. The characters are at the heart of the world's first great empire, and what exists beyond the incomprehensibly vast (from their perspective) territory claimed by the Shan'iatu is largely irrelevant. In keeping with this theme, I don't imagine Irem carrying out much trade outside of its own borders. Despite the existence of relics that allow for transportation to anywhere in the world, I have the empire being far more reliant on mundane travelling, and that means the constrains of geography keep them from going too far past the borders described in the books. Certainly no contact with the Americas, I doubt they even reached the Western Mediterranean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:04:15-08:00","id":417270,"title":"","content":"To me, even if they did reach the other side of the Mediterranean they wouldn't find anything interesting there except a bunch of cavemen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:59:58-08:00","id":417299,"title":"","content":"Also that. Not much point in trading if what they have to offer is flint tools while you're carting around an arsenal of magic bronze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:03:31-08:00","id":417755,"title":"","content":"Colonial 'trading' is less about actual trading more about the more advanced and sophisticated power coming and taking whatever they want. The Iremites aren't after the flint tools, they're offer more exotic resources... whatever the Iremite equivelent of oil, rare earths or uranium is.In that situation, dealing with cavemen is actually preferable. You simply enslave them, or hire them for a few rocks and beans, and then essentially steal all of the resources they don't know how to use to fuel your ever-growing exploitative empire. Not only do they have no chance of resisting you, they don't even appreciate the value of the theft itself because they didn't have any idea how to use the uranium in the first place.<br /> <br /> ... until you meat Ubar, and go, 'whoops'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:20:02-08:00","id":417769,"title":"","content":"Which is, presumably, what the empire was doing throughout the expansionist segment of its existence and how it ended up owning a swathe of the Middle East and Africa. Trade beyond the empire's borders described in the core book remains a rather pointless prospect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T06:31:39-08:00","id":421683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.crystalinks.com/gc_egyptconnection.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.crystalinks.com/IsisTempleGrandCanyon.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.crystalinks.com/gc_egyptconnection.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Grand Canyon - Egyptian Influences - Crystalinks - Crystalinks </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.crystalinks.com/gc_egyptconnection.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.crystalinks.com/gc_egyptconnection.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It might make a good place to house your dead, though...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:07:27-07:00","id":467819,"title":"","content":"Sothis Ascends hints at the old African Olmec theory, which is definitely interesting. It also describes the Ki-En-Gir (proto-Sumeria) as having empire, sorcery, and language all their own, independent of Shan'iatu meddling.<br /> <br /> I could definitely see a rare few Alchemists going far, far north in search of tin.<br /> <br /> Opening up the crossover can of worms means we could see small groups using High Speech and Awakened magic or the First Tongue of spirits (since we now know the Sundering in WtF takes place a few hundred years before Irem) as potent enemies during the time of the Nameless Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-03-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:26:30-07:00","id":467830,"title":"","content":"Irem versus Kush seems like it's be a real bundle of laughs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:39:52-07:00","id":468086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/415916-irem-and-distant-trade?p=467819#post467819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sothis Ascends hints at the old African Olmec theory, which is definitely interesting. It also describes the Ki-En-Gir (proto-Sumeria) as having empire, sorcery, and language all their own, independent of Shan'iatu meddling.<br /> <br /> I could definitely see a rare few Alchemists going far, far north in search of tin.<br /> <br /> Opening up the crossover can of worms means we could see small groups using High Speech and Awakened magic or the First Tongue of spirits (since we now know the Sundering in WtF takes place a few hundred years before Irem) as potent enemies during the time of the Nameless Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum, Kin-En-Gir seemed to not be an Empire at the time, they were more like a collection of a few independent city-states, in the World of Darkness, the Nameless Empire was the first one.(If you not count Atlantis that is)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T09:00:12-07:00","id":468444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/415916-irem-and-distant-trade?p=417270#post417270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, even if they did reach the other side of the Mediterranean they wouldn't find anything interesting there except a bunch of cavemen</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They were Neolithic, not Paleolithic - there was agriculture and wood construction. There's even some copper tool use (though still pre-Bronze).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T09:07:01-07:00","id":468447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/415916-irem-and-distant-trade?p=415999#post415999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> semi-mythical Xia Dynasty of China.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see the Xia explored as a mythic empire setting ala Irem, Kush, and what we're getting for the Vinca - but it's dated 2070-1600 bce, long after the fall of Irem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:19:48-07:00","id":506401,"title":"","content":"In the New Kingdom Egypt built an empire on the vassal system- all the occupied kingdoms (with the important exception of Nubia and surrounding lands) were left to their own devices as long as they gave proper tribute to the Pharaoh and sent their children to Egypt for education (Re: allowed them to be used as hostages by the Egyptians, to be executed should the vassals attempt rebellion). I imagine this makes the most logical sense for the Irem Empire as well.<br /> <br /> On a more Lovecraftian note, I've long assumed that Irem encountered several rival empires in its time. Most of them were petty human kingdoms that fell easily to conquest. One was a society based on magic wholly different from Shaniatu, and there were many terrible wars and treaties with the Atlanteans. And then there were....other empires. Empires more ancient than humanity, ruled by things that defied description. Empires who used humanity not even as servants or slaves but as raw materials...twisting body and mind and soul into &quot;better&quot; forms more pleasing to their masters. As terrible as Irem is, the world does owe them this much....those empires it could eradicate, it did so without mercy or hesitation. Those it could not....it stole away names to send its denizens into realms beyond the Earth. Those that resisted both of these were put to sleep, their lands scoured and poisoned so that none but the most insane would dare to venture there. Alas, as the Arisen awake in cycles, so too are these enchantments tied to the stars. One day the forgotten empires will rise again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T20:36:26-07:00","id":507575,"title":"","content":"In regard to the trans atlantic part,<a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_19769_5-baffling-discoveries-that-prove-history-books-are-wrong.html\" target=\"_blank\"> they have found traces of cocaine and tobacco in Egyptian mummies</a> and even found tobacco leaves and tobacco beetles in the gut of Ramses the 2nd. So it's looking like Egypt did indeed have transatlantic trade. Question is, was that trade going on in Irem's time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T08:48:48-07:00","id":508129,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't take my revisionist history from Craked. A 2-second wikipedia search would have revealed the problems with their claim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T13:16:48-07:00","id":508363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/415916-irem-and-distant-trade?p=508129#post508129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't take my revisionist history from Craked. A 2-second wikipedia search would have revealed the problems with their claim.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories#Claims_involving_African_contact\" target=\"_blank\">Yeah, I looked it up</a> and now I see the holes in the theory. Still, just because it probably isn't true in our world doesn't mean it's not true in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T13:38:06-07:00","id":508372,"title":"","content":"That's true enough. Plus Irem has magic which makes things a lot easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T21:55:43-07:00","id":583187,"title":"","content":"I would love to see more interesting empires and cultures from the time of Irem, so I'm totally onboard for that one! But for me trans-atlantic trade with that level of naval technology would require a serious ammount of magic, kind of Atlantis-style to it, and thus I feel that its a bit to much. But other Mediterranean, African, Indian etc. cultures should work wonders in this regards. The main question I see is how to bring them into the game without them steeping on Irem's toes as the great necromancers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T23:20:44-07:00","id":584285,"title":"","content":"Atamajakki makes a good point about tin; it's significantly rarer than copper and very desirable for making bronze. Arsenical bronze is easier to make, since many bronze ores contain arsenic anyway, but has serious health drawbacks... not that the Shan'iatu necessarily cared. Nevertheless, I could see the Guild of Alchemists having a vested interest in seeking the stuff out, and the nearest viable sources are pretty far away. If early Imperial roman sources are to be believed, the Greeks were aware of Cornwall at least as early as the 4th century BCE, when the local Britons traded tin and bronze ore with &quot;foreign merchants.&quot;<br /> <br /> If we suppose that some Iremites were willing to travel a similar distance in order to acquire tin, it's possible that some would have followed the west African coast southward. If they devoted a lot of effort to exploring that coast, they may have discovered the &quot;volta do mar&quot; navigational technique, which involves sailing out into the Atlantic rather than closely following the coast, in order to take advantage of favorable ocean and wind currents. I'm not sure it's really possible to take advantage of that technique without the lateen sail, but lets assume for the moment that you get some advantage even with a single square sail like the Iremites would presumably be using.<br /> <br /> If the Iremites were using the volta, and they kept at their African exploration (perhaps after discovering that west Africa was quite rich in gold), then they might just have stumbled across Brazil in the same way that Pedro \u00c1lvares Cabral would many thousands of years later. And then, if they decided there was something they wanted in this new territory, they might have explored more of the Americas.<br /> <br /> That's a lot of ifs, but it's about the most plausible scenario for bronze age trans-Atlantic contact that I can think of, besides &quot;a wizard did it.&quot; The Iremites could theoretically also have done what Thor Heyerdahl did with his <i>Ra II</i> and crossed further north by taking advantage of the Canary Current, but Heyerdahl had the advantage of knowing not only that there was something on the other side of the ocean, but also exactly how far away it was. Without some kind of really accurate divination, it would be next to impossible to plan a similar voyage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:19:14-07:00","id":585579,"title":"","content":"I've said this before, but if you are willing to put aside reason and embrace more imaginative narratives, there is some evidence to support a colonial Irem:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scota\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/02_Queen_Scota_Unfurls_the_Sacred_Banner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scota\" target=\"_blank\"> Scota - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scota\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scota </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/ancientegyptiansinamerica/ancient-egyptians-grand-canyon\" target=\"_blank\">https://sites.google.com/site/ancien...s-grand-canyon</a><br /> <br /> A more &quot;historical&quot; idea would be to match the Nameless Empire with the common practices of actual Ancient Egypt. And historical Egyptians didn't like to go beyond the heartland, and the Nile was so prosperous they had little need to. When they did want to contact foreign lands, they usually employed an intermediary like the Phoenicians (who are credited with the first circumnavigation of Africa at the behest of Pharaoh Nekau II, for instance). So perhaps a mysterious third party of merchant seamen is called for if we want to lengthen the reach of Irem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T22:40:59-07:00","id":585671,"title":"","content":"Oh no! But if the Iremites were in the Grand Canyon, they would surely have eventually run afoul of the super-advanced lizard people who ruled the American Southwest until around 5000 years ago. Or... wait... maybe it was the sorcery of Irem that ultimately drove them to <a href=\"http://documents.latimes.com/jan-29-1934-lizard-people/\" target=\"_blank\">flee underground beneath what would one day become Los Angeles</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:51:12-07:00","id":586304,"title":"","content":"Well, Mummy hints in several places that Irem shared the world with strange and sinister entities. There's the Chthonic Beast in the Core Book, Ancestry of Forgotten Stars from Guildhalls of the Deathless, and the Black Angels/the origin of the Rotting Temple in Book of the Deceived. So yeah, strange lizard people could be appropriate, depending on where you take your inspiration from- <a href=\"http://www.dagonbytes.com/thelibrary/lovecraft/thenamelesscity.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dagonbytes.com/thelibrary...melesscity.htm</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T20:00:10-07:00","id":586719,"title":"","content":"Lovecraft is, of course, an old standby when it comes to horrible ancient things waking up and starting cults and such; I just thought people might be interested in the link I posted, since it's a somewhat obscure bit of eccentricity that's certainly given me game ideas...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T01:50:02-07:00","id":623994,"title":"","content":"On another note, this might make a good location for lost Irem. Supposedly the oldest ruins in Egypt (and maybe Africa) are found here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nabta_Playa#Early_history\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Calendar_aswan.JPG/1280px-Calendar_aswan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nabta_Playa#Early_history\" target=\"_blank\"> Nabta Playa - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nabta_Playa#Early_history\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nabta_Playa#Early_history </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T23:15:27-08:00","id":770557,"title":"","content":"I believe Guildhalls of the Deathless alludes to an unknown force/group working to keep the Arisen out of Asia; any ideas for who or what would know enough about the servants of Irem to oppose them, and what would be powerful enough to do so successfully?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T02:45:52-08:00","id":770612,"title":"","content":"I don't remember that. Any idea what section it was in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T12:14:28-08:00","id":770883,"title":"","content":"I want to say it's in the Asia section for the Maa-Kep? It's one throwaway line that caught my eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T13:31:15-08:00","id":770918,"title":"","content":"Do you mean this closing paragraph from the Su-Menent write up on Asia?<br /> <br /> &quot;Of the second issue, the adversaries they face, the so called Orient has long had supernatural creatures who actively fight to keep supernatural expats out of their backyard. The times grow less perilous, but the Arisen face a constant threat. It\u2019s become easier to maintain small cults and a low profile than risk angering the locals.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T16:43:43-08:00","id":771059,"title":"","content":"That would be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T18:15:53-08:00","id":771108,"title":"","content":"In descending order of preference, I would say the main enemies of Arisen migration into the East are:<br /> <br /> 1. First wave Arisen who, like their American counterparts, have &quot;gone native&quot; and largely adopted the trappings of one far east culture or another. Since the Capacocha of Mummy: The Resurrection somewhat live on in the Rio setting (viz the first wave mummies assimilated into the native culture) the same should happen for the Wu Tian mummies (in my opinion, anyway). Perhaps the &quot;Oriental&quot; Arisen know what happened to their South American counterparts and have taken steps to keep &quot;foreign&quot; Arisen out of their adopted homes?<br /> <br /> 2. Unique forms of Lifeless. There are plenty of cultures that practiced one form of mummification or another in the far east, from the First Emperor of China seeking a potion of immortality right on into certain modern sects of Buddhists practicing ritual mummification to this day. Combine that with local traditions of walking dead and you have plenty of potential entities capable of becoming Lifeless. <br /> <br /> 3. Mortal cultists, whether out and out Scorpion Cults or an enemy the Mummies made at some point in the last 6000 years (a long time to make any number of enemies from cultures ancient and modern). Perhaps one of the Taoist Immortal circles from the WOD: Immortal or WOD: Sixth Sense books? Perhaps a sect that deals with Reincarnation (could be Hindu, Buddhist, etc) finds the notion of immortal, changeless, undying souls fundamentally corrupt and hunts them at every turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T07:33:23-08:00","id":775455,"title":"","content":"Well... didn't some dark, horrible cloud rise up from the east in the last Sothic turn? Plus, it isn't hard to imagine that East, being opposite of their journey west, is inauspicious. Though, as an ozophile, II'm more interested in why Australia is often no man's land, in modern times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T13:55:51-08:00","id":775618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/415916-irem-and-distant-trade?p=775455#post775455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... didn't some dark, horrible cloud rise up from the east in the last Sothic turn? Plus, it isn't hard to imagine that East, being opposite of their journey west, is inauspicious. Though, as an ozophile, II'm more interested in why Australia is often no man's land, in modern times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the &quot;ominous cloud&quot; is talking about this <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extreme_weather_events_of_535%E2%80%93536\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extrem...35%E2%80%93536</a><br /> <br /> Also, East is the direction of the rising sun, so considered the direction of life and rebirth. That's why the necropolis was generally on the western end of the Nile and the people were generally on the Eastern end. Which might be a taboo since mummies are basically &quot;the dead&quot;, but also might be a holy direction since they return like the sunrise and set in a similar cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}